---
import Prose from './Prose.astro';
import Callout from './Callout.astro';
import { CODE_TOOLS } from '../data/guide';
---

<Prose class="max-w-none">
  <p>
    Three files keep the codebase consistent and reproducible. Each does one job and stays out of
    the others' way.
  </p>

  {CODE_TOOLS.map((tool) => (
    <>
      <h3>{tool.name}</h3>
      <p>{tool.what}</p>
      <p>
        <strong>In TechCart:</strong> {tool.techcart}
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Why it matters:</strong> {tool.why}
      </p>
    </>
  ))}

  <Callout type="note">
    ESLint and Prettier are kept in separate lanes — ESLint for correctness, Prettier for
    formatting. Wiring Prettier in as an ESLint rule (eslint-plugin-prettier) makes the two fight
    and slows the lint run down.
  </Callout>
</Prose>
